|passage=[T]he ''grubit'' bombs went rolling back and forth over our feet, fetching up against the sides of the car with a crash. The big Red Guard, whose name was Vladimir Nicolaievitch, plied me with questions about America {{...}} while we held on to each other and danced amid the '''caroming''' bombs.}}

